WEBVTT

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.430
HYAKKO PARTY DRIVEN INTO CORNER

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.180
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.640
<i>I'll say it as many times as you wish</i>
<i>to help you understand.</i>

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.150
You've caused too many incidents
without any careful thought...

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.110
It's only a matter of time
before the authorities

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.770
put the whole picture together.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.780
Hence, Mr. Kershner will terminate
his financial aid to you immediately.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.500
This is how you treat us
after all that we've done for you?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.000
Is this how you do things?

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.880
As one who has pushed
xenophobic principles

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.090
while collaborating with us,
you have no right to say that.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.130
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.300
We've never received help
from you savages.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:57.850
We merely played along with the
vagary of you monsters, that's all.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.230
We need to solve the problem

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.940
before the restoration
of Showa takes place.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.240
It's time to exterminate the monsters.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:57.020
It's so heavy!

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.100
Good work.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.100
Why aren't you working, too?

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.900
I'm the intellectual type.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:03.900
That's strange.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.780
-Huh?
-The Hyakko Party, I mean.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:09.650
They haven't been attacking scholars
and doctors lately.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:13.280
Certainly not since
the Vampires attacked Dr. Hanada.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.660
Which means they've collected
all the parts they needed...

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:21.080
Philip, bring me the investigation
file that we borrowed yesterday.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.210
What? Seriously?

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.380
I'll bring it.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.300
He seems rather proactive.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.930
I guess he's feeling better now.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:37.640
At any rate, that's good news.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:40.230
Excuse me.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.190
Hello, Ryoko.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.440
My father would like to
invite you to dinner tonight.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.650
I've a feeling it's gonna be
formal and uncomfortable.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.900
You don't know anything about
table manners, do you, little boy?

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:56.660
What? Yes, I do!
I'll show you my elegant table manners!

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.660
Professor and everyone here
would love to join you tonight.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.710
Great. I'll tell my father that you...

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.170
What's wrong, Ryoko?

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.880
Nothing. Well,
I look forward to seeing you all tonight.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:17.100
-Is this what you needed?
-Yes. Thanks

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.970
Do you need anything else?

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.140
That's all for now.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:22.850
Okay.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.480
-Did you just see that?
-Totally.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.360
Hey. See what?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:35.820
I wasn't expecting our competitor,
V Shipping, to pay us a visit.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.240
Please.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.410
Businessmen like us working hard
in distant countries

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.620
need to cooperate with one another.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:46.960
With pleasure, but the kind of merchandise
that we handle at the moment

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.800
has nothing to do with your expertise.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.960
Namely, export of weapons and technology?

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.470
Alma Trading Company
always looks 10 to 20 years ahead...

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:00.850
Thanks to that, we're now beginning

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:03.480
to strengthen our ties
with this country's army.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.230
That's an enviable position.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.230
Oh, please.
V Shipping's profits are steadily...

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.410
Excuse me. That was close.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.460
Well, well. You're...

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:37.470
Excuse me for suddenly talking to you
on your way out the other day...

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.260
But what a coincidence
to run into you here...

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:42.930
Inspecting on your rival, I see.
I admire your dedication.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.390
What did you think
of Alma Trading Company?

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:48.560
We simply discussed about
the future of the shipping industry

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.020
as fellow traders.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.480
Oh, come on.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:55.360
Oh, by the way.
About Dr. Kisuke Hanada going missing...

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.400
Was everything all right?

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:01.240
I heard that an employee of yours
was involved in the incident.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.830
Everything is fine...

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:06.500
But your ability to collect information
is impressive for a news writer.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.080
This is my specialty after all...

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:12.960
You hear things
whether you want to or not.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:17.220
For example, I heard that
Dr. Hanada didn't go missing,

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:18.170
but was murdered.

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:26.730
You were rushing over to
the doctor's home that day, weren't you?

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:35.530
You need to make your cover-up job
seem more convincing. Mr. Willard.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:37.690
The same goes for you, too.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.790
Alma Trading Company and V Shipping...

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.580
The latter is more suspicious, but...

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:59.300
<i>A guy who's supposed to be in Harbin</i>

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:01.890
<i>was wandering around</i>
<i>in Ginza in plain clothes...</i>

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.800
<i>I couldn't resist talking to you.</i>

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:05.260
I'm honored.

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:06.970
I see that it's an urgent matter

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:10.640
-considering that they waved you back.
-Yes. They are working me hard...

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.770
By the way, congratulations
on your promotion

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:16.690
to Director of Bureau of Weapons,
Major General Kakizaki.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:19.070
You know everything don't you?

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.410
I visited Ichigayadai earlier
to give the new principal

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:24.280
my words of encouragement.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:29.290
I was lucky to have been a
student while you taught there.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:32.330
Are you off to another place
to give a pep talk?

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:35.000
No. I'm off to Gotemba for inspection.

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:38.380
You're personally going to an inspection?

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:41.760
Is it some kind of drill to test a
new weapon at the same time?

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.180
It's classified,
so I can't discuss the matter.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.010
-Forgive me.
-That's fine.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:47.600
However, Iba,

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:52.350
it's something that could
change the very nature of war.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:56.730
It probably would have been impossible
for Japan to develop it solely on its own.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.110
Was it Alma Trading Company?

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:04.200
It seems recommending you
to intelligence was the right choice.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.950
There will certainly be another war.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:11.960
<i>If that thing gets put to use,</i>

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:14.250
<i>we wouldn't have to waste</i>
<i>the lives of soldiers</i>

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:17.290
<i>like we did against the Chinese,</i>
<i>the Russians, or in Europe.</i>

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:21.590
<i>We absolutely must make this drill</i>
<i>a success.</i>

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:27.010
The police force raided the hideout
of the Hyakko Party,

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.100
but they had already escaped.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:30.600
Did they leave anything?

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:34.100
Nothing. But according to the report
there were signs of confrontation,

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:36.600
and an ash-like substance
was scattered all over the place.

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.440
So, they were working together
with the Vampires, after all.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.320
But what could have
caused the internal discord?

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.070
They must have used the Hyakko Party
to collect the parts,

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:47.370
but once they got them,
they didn't need them any longer.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:50.370
The question is
what they did with those parts.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.040
Are you thinking Alma Trading Company?

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.830
Huh? That's where the collected parts are?

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:57.790
What did you find out?

00:08:57.880 --> 00:08:59.960
It was a motivated, good-natured company.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:02.760
They are trying to sell a new weapon
to the army.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:06.340
The executive even told me about a drill
scheduled to take place in Shizuoka.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:11.390
I wonder if the good-natured staff
know that the new weapon

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:12.850
is smeared in blood.

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:14.640
Probably not...

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:17.980
But they are certainly behind all of this.

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.440
They might show up at the military drill.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.030
This could be the opportunity
to kill the Royals.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:27.070
I can barely wait... And?
What do we do about the Hyakko Party?

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:30.950
The Vampires sold them out. I don't think
the Hyakko Party would leave them alone.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:34.830
-Shall we split up into two groups?
-Professor.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:44.880
Mochizuki. Get me a ticket
to Gotemba immediately.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:48.050
Gotemba?
You're leaving the imperial capital?

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:50.390
I need to see
what Alma Trading Company is up to.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:54.180
Alma? Then what do we do about V Shipping?

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:57.690
It wouldn't be fair
if we didn't harass both groups equally.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.610
V Shipping and Alma Trading Company...

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.730
<i>What are they planning to do</i>
<i>in this country?</i>

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:11.450
Excellent table manners, little boy.

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:13.660
I don't know how to use chopsticks...

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.250
Besides, this is raw!!

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:21.500
You don't like Japanese food, I take it.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:22.840
Quite the contrary.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:26.630
Only in Japan
could we enjoy fish so fresh.

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:30.760
We're also happy to have dinner
with so many people...

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:33.720
My wife passed away quite early.

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:36.180
Usually, it's just my daughter and I.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:40.810
That's strange, Ryoko. You usually eat
at least three bowls of rice.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:43.310
Fa...Father!!

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.150
Sorry.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:47.820
By the way, professor. How's work coming?

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.280
You seem very busy every day.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:53.910
It could not have been possible without
your kind gesture to allow us to stay.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.660
For your information,

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.250
I will send my subordinates
on a mission tomorrow.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:00.000
I see. Where will they go?

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:01.920
To Gotemba in Shizuoka...

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:05.090
We have become quite intimate
with a certain client.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.380
Um... who exactly is going?

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:09.720
I am.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:11.800
What's wrong, Ryoko?

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:12.930
Nothing.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.180
Don't worry, Ryoko.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:18.850
I will take good care of Yuliy.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:22.900
That's right. Yuliy will be just fine.
I mean, look at him.

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:27.360
Um... let's just continue eating.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:29.940
What a strange girl.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:34.160
Stay away from me.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:56.760
How could this be possible?

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:58.390
Major General Kakizaki.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:01.770
Do you like our new product?

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:06.520
We look forward to continue
doing business with you.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:19.370
<i>The Ark of Sirius?</i>

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:22.500
You still speak of such nonsense?

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:25.420
I wouldn't call it nonsense...

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:30.050
It is the foundation
that promises our prosperity.

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:35.130
Listen to this man who's clinging on
to the treasure of filthy wolves.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:39.430
Are you telling me then
to watch our kind die out

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:42.100
without doing anything?

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:45.900
If that is our destiny, so be it.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:48.980
Not so fast, Yevgraf...

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:50.780
Show some respect.

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:52.990
There's no point in talking with you.

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:57.620
Master Yev.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:01.370
-Master Yev. Master Yev.
-Guess what?

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:07.290
That's good news.

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:13.170
Those old fools have lost their pride
as Vampires.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:17.760
If they wish to perish,
then they may perish alone.

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.990
<i>Oh, great.</i>
<i>I just had to follow him, didn't I?</i>

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.540
-What?
-It's nothing.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.500
What is it?

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:56.970
Fine, then. I was wondering
why you volunteered to go on this mission.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:13:59.430
No reason in particular.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:02.680
I just thought I would get to kill
many Vampires. That's all.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.850
What's the big rush?

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.310
I have no time to waste.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.150
I can't just sit and wait patiently.

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:13.070
-Plus...
-Plus what?

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:15.820
No. It's nothing.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:22.450
<i>Plus....</i>
<i>I might be able to see my brother.</i>

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:27.830
I think serving alcohol in the afternoon
would bring in more customers.

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:31.790
If business gets too good here,
I'd have difficulty doing my other job

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.210
I'm very happy.

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.090
I can finally contribute
to my organization.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:41.970
<i>Don't get too passionate.</i>

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:45.600
<i>They are not like human villains.</i>

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:56.280
That's great to hear. Yes, truly.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:06.870
What's going on here?

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:14.000
Divine punishment.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.840
There are two types of Vampires:
the aristocrat class called the Royals,

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:20.380
and the class that serves them,
called the Slaves.

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:22.590
That's how we categorize them...

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:25.260
Slaves disguise themselves as humans,

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:27.430
and protect their eyes
with special lenses...

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:31.890
Without the lenses, sunlight would
instantly turn them into ashes.

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:33.190
And the Royals?

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:35.480
They have high combative abilities

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:37.360
even when they are
not in their original form,

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:40.360
plus they are capable of moving freely
under the sun without limitation...

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:44.910
And they live among us nonchalantly.

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:46.870
That's frightening.

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:49.620
So, what did you find out?

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:54.540
Yes... The Hyakko Party, which has nowhere
to hide anymore in the imperial capital,

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:57.550
has also lost financial aid
from their sponsor recently.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:59.590
Who's the sponsor?

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:01.590
Just as you predicted.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:03.970
Alma Trading Company.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:08.930
Let me use your phone.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.310
Strange...

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:16.150
Master.
The corpses aren't turning into ashes.

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.400
Perhaps they still aren't dead.

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:24.360
Those monsters.
They hired humans with money like we do.

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:32.410
-Where is Kershner?
-I don't know!

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:38.460
-I want Kershner.
-The vice president went to Gotemba

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.420
to watch an experiment of a new weapon.

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:41.760
A new weapon?

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:44.800
Tell me more.

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:49.180
We'll be here until they couple a car
in order to cross the mountain.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:50.100
I see.

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:55.600
Well, well. Seems we're on the same train!

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:57.860
I'm on my way to Hakone!

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:00.860
That's not it.

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:02.440
Wow. That looks delicious.

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:06.160
Don't eat hurriedly.
You got rice on your face.

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:08.870
I bought some lunch boxes earlier.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:11.290
Would you all like some?

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.000
That's it.

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:16.210
Put me through.

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:17.540
<i>Major?</i>

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:18.880
Yes. It's me.

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.300
-How's it going--
<i>-There's been a big accident</i>

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:22.210
<i>at the drill in Fuji!</i>

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:24.260
Mochizuki. Calm down now.

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:27.930
<i>Like I said, the infantry battalion</i>
<i>at Fuji has been annihilated.</i>

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:28.840
What?

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:32.310
We've intercepted a radio message
from Gotemba to the central command room.

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:36.520
At around 8:30 last night, an accident
of some sort occurred during the drill

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.230
at the Fuji Susono Maneuvering Ground...

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:40.940
<i>All participating officers were killed.</i>

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:43.440
What happened to Major General Kakizaki?

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:46.530
<i>He's safe. It seems he has</i>
<i>already left on a special train</i>

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:48.700
<i>for the imperial capital</i>
<i>to report to the Emperor.</i>

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:54.450
By train?

00:17:57.670 --> 00:18:00.130
<i>Major. Major Iba?</i>

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:03.130
What is it, Yuliy?

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:08.510
I smell blood.

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.050
Hey. Wait, Yuliy.

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:13.890
Thank you very much.

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.020
Yuliy. Wait.

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:47.510
Everyone was killed?

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.590
-Professor.
-Sorry we're late.

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:52.300
I heard the Hyakko Party did it.
This is terrible.

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:54.260
In broad daylight?

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:57.560
They came to ask for money,
but were refused perhaps?

00:18:58.020 --> 00:18:59.810
If they didn't get money, what next?

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:01.770
Real estate, goods...

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:03.940
Professor?

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.400
We need to hurry and meet up with Yuliy.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:16.410
-Did Yuliy forget something in Tokyo?
-Excuse me...

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:18.910
Ticket please.

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:22.710
Oh, I'm sorry. I changed trains...

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:24.540
May I buy the ticket here?

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:28.380
No...

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.880
I'll check my bag...

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:40.940
Would you like one?

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:51.280
Stop. Who are you!?

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:53.450
I'm Iba of the General Staff Office.

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:55.700
I got on at Kozu for a special mission.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:57.330
Sir.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.410
Where is Major General Kakizaki?

00:20:12.590 --> 00:20:14.760
Here. Your new ticket.

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:16.260
Thank you.

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:18.930
Now, How are we going to explain
to the professor

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:21.480
about suddenly abandoning the mission?

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:24.730
There's a Vampire on this train.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:28.190
I can't follow the smell anymore
because of the smoke,

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:29.860
but I'm sure of it.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.700
It would be a mess
if we have to fight here.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:40.040
I'll go see how many passengers we have
and their positions... You stay here.

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:42.460
-No. I'm coming, too.
-Stay here.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.580
I can't have you hopping on
to some other train again.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:47.920
All right.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:49.130
Be good.

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:02.480
The experiment ended so quickly
that I couldn't even get any useful data.

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:05.060
The result is the proof of all proofs.

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.690
Wow. It's been certified
by Master Kershner!

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:12.070
Then we shall get ready
for mass production

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:14.280
once we get back to Tokyo, yes!?

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:19.740
I can't believe we have to
depend on a man like him...

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:24.370
But why is Master Yevgraf
so interested in the Ark

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:27.420
whose existence hasn't even been proven?

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:34.470
<i>I'd choose certainty over clinging on</i>
<i>to an uncertain existence.</i>

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:07.960
Thank you.

00:22:23.720 --> 00:22:24.890
EPISODE 4
BEGINNING OF TRICKERY

00:24:02.150 --> 00:24:05.660
<i>-Oh, you're that creep from the other day.</i>
<i>-Aren't you a Vampire?</i>

00:24:05.740 --> 00:24:07.830
<i>10 years... that's quite a detour.</i>

00:24:07.910 --> 00:24:10.870
<i>-I guess it's showtime!</i>
<i>-I'll put you out of your misery.</i>

00:24:10.950 --> 00:24:11.960
EPISODE 5
THE FRANKENSTEIN

00:24:19.960 --> 00:24:24.970
Subtitle translation by Kozo Komori
